    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There's just one test class (`AcceptanceTest`, plus two support classes), and it passes along with the compile of all generated/main code.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` raw E.164.\n\n**Three small, cohesive changes:**\n\n1. **`util/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-purpose helper holding all the formatting logic: splits the known country code (`+61`/`+1`) and groups the national digits in threes via a regex (`\"+61412345678\"` \u2192 `\"+61 412 345 678\"`). New class \u2192 near-zero surrounding complexity.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one tiny `@AfterMapping` method (`deriveTelephoneDisplay`, CC 1, one statement) that delegates to the helper, matching the existing `deriveHouseholdId`/`deriveLocality`/etc. pattern. No logic lives here, so its cost is just the single delegating line.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the setter/field.\n\n**Structural-impact rationale:** the CC-heavy work sits in the brand-new `TelephoneDisplay` class (WMC_other \u2248 0), and the only edit to the high-WMC `OwnerMapper` is a trivial one-line delegating method \u2014 so no existing function grows in complexity and the expensive `WMC_other \u00d7 CC \u00d7 lines` term stays small everywhere.",
